    "body": "The new Hyundai IONIQ 6 is now on sale in the UK with an impressive range of up to 422 miles, starting at about $45,000.\nHyundai reveals new IONIQ 6 prices and range in the UK\nHyundai opened orders for the all-new IONIQ 6 in the UK, starting at £33,240 ($45,000), including the Electric Car Grant (ECG).\nThe “evolved” electrified streamliner brings a sharp new design, a refined interior, and a bigger battery for longer range.\nHyundai “enhanced every line and detail” for a cleaner, stronger silhouette. The front includes a redesigned shark nose and slim daytime running lights, while the black lower body garnish now extends into the doors.\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nThe rear features a new extended ducktail design replacing the previous generation’s prominent spoiler.\nInside, Hyundai overhauled the new IONIQ 6’s interior with a redesigned two-tone leather steering wheel, a digital side mirror, and a “bridge-type” center console that includes a wireless phone charger and physical buttons.\nIt includes Hyundai’s new infotainment setup, including dual 12.3″ navigation and infotainment screens with wireless Apple CarPlay and Android Auto capabilities.\nNew Hyundai IONIQ 6 N-Line interior (Source: Hyundai UK)\nIn the UK, the new IONIQ 6 is available in three trims: Premium, N-Line, and N-Line Evo, with 225 horsepower RWD or 320 horsepower AWD powertrains.\nThe base Hyundai IONIQ 6 Premium uses a new 84 kWh battery with the 225 hp RWD powertrain, delivering up to 422 miles of range and 4.6 miles/kWh efficiency.\nIt starts at £33,240 with the ECG. It includes 18″ alloy wheels, flush auto door handles, dual-zone climate control, heated front seats, heated steering wheel, heat pump, smart regenerative braking, wireless phone charging, over-the-air updates, and the full suite of key safety systems.\nThe IONIQ 6 N-Line starts at £36,240, including the ECG, and adds a more dynamic N-Line exterior and interior design.\nUpgrading to the range-topping N-Line Evo costs £43,270 and adds features like leather and suede seat trim, a suede headliner, front relaxation seats, ventilated front seats, an electric sunroof, and a head-up display.\nNew Hyundai IONIQ 6 (Source: Hyundai UK)\nOther added features included with the N-Line Evo trim include Surround View Monitor, Remote Smart Parking Assist, Parking Collision Avoidance Assist, Digital Key 2, Walk-Away Lock, exterior Vehicle-to-Load adaptor, and BOSE premium audio.\nBoth the IONIQ 6 N-Line and N-Line Evo use the 84 kWh battery, providing up to 364 miles of driving range in RWD and up to 354 miles with the AWD powertrain.\nNew Hyundai IONIQ 6 trim | UK prices and Electric Car Grant, OTR | Driving Range\nIONIQ 6 Premium 84kWh RWD | £33,240 inc ECG | 422 miles\nIONIQ 6 N Line 84kWh RWD | £36,240 inc ECG | 364 miles\nIONIQ 6 N Line 84kWh AWD | £43,490 | 354 miles\nIONIQ 6 N Line Evo 84kWh RWD | £43,270 | 364 miles\nIONIQ 6 N Line Evo 84kWh AWD | £46,770 | 354 miles\nNew Hyundai IONIQ 6 prices in the UK\nTop comment by OrangeFlask\nLiked by 0 people\nBeautiful car, very efficient and from what I read, very comfortable. I had my eyes set on it, but the small trunk was a dealbreaker for me. So I went for the EV6, which is maybe even more of a stunner (in the eyes of the beholder) but admittedly significantly less efficient.\nView all comments\nThanks to its 800-volt electrical architecture, the IONIQ 6’s battery can charge from 10% to 80% in about 18 minutes at DC fast-charging speeds of up to 350 kW.\nThe new IONIQ 6 is now available to order on Hyundai UK’s website, with deliveries set to begin in early 2027.\nSadly, those in the US will miss out on the new-and-improved electrified streamliner. Hyundai is discontinuing the standard IONIQ 6 in the US after the 2026 model year, while the performance N will remain on sale.\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on X , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
